    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy, we need to consider the choices available for each category (entrees, drinks, and desserts) and then multiply these choices together.\n\n1. **Entrees:**\n   - There are 4 entrees available.\n   - So, Crystal has 4 choices for the entree.\n\n2. **Drinks:**\n   - There are 2 drinks available.\n   - So, Crystal has 2 choices for the drink.\n\n3. **Desserts:**\n   - There are 2 desserts available.\n   - So, Crystal has 2 choices for the dessert.\n\nTo find the total number of distinct possible meals, we multiply the number of choices for each category:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of meals} = (\\text{Number of entrees}) \\times (\\text{Number of drinks}) \\times (\\text{Number of desserts})\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the values we have:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of meals} = 4 \\times 2 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nCalculating the product:\n\n\\[\n4 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\\[\n8 \\times 2 = 16\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).",
